            <h2 class="h4 mb-4 text-info">
              What is really going on inside America’s traveler information systems, and how to buy one that lasts.
            </h2>
            <p>
              511 was built for a world where you picked up a phone to ask whether the freeway was jammed. That world is gone, and
              the data infrastructure underneath these systems has matured dramatically in the last twenty years. This guide is a
              California-informed look at what has actually changed, written for the people who fund, procure, and run these
              systems.
            </p>

